# Map_Design — Skeleton

## 1. Applies when
Competitive or session-based games with authored arenas (multiplayer_shooter, strategy).

## 2. This document owns
- Arena layout intent: lanes, sightlines, choke points, verticality, callout naming.
- Mode-coverage analysis (which modes a map serves) and pacing zones.
- Rotation/respawn geometry rationale.

## 3. This document does NOT own
- Single-player level content and beats — Level_Design.
- Persistent open-world structure — World_Design.
- Encounter composition placed on the map — Encounter_Design.

## 4. Recommended chapter structure
1. Map intent / 2. Layout & zones / 3. Lanes & sightlines / 4. Modes covered / 5. Spawns & rotation / 6. Verticality / 7. Callouts / 8. Balance watchlist / 9. Open questions

## 5. Common boundaries
- Map_Design vs Level_Design: repeated competitive spaces vs authored one-shot spaces.
- Map_Design vs World_Design: session arena vs persistent world.

## 6. Common audit rules
- Every zone referenced by an encounter/mode exists in the layout chapter.
- Callout names come from Naming; this document only applies them.
